    "reason": "Two relative clauses are compressed: 'the standard libraries ship' and 'empirical ... analysis motivates'; splitting them makes the threshold and its motivation clear."
  },
  {
    "find": "Keeping the ratio bounded is what preserves amortized O(1) access guarantees, which unbounded chain-length growth would otherwise erode.",
    "replace": "Keeping the ratio bounded preserves amortized O(1) access guarantees. Otherwise, chains growing without bound would weaken those guarantees.",
    "type": "noun-stack",
    "reason": "The noun stack 'unbounded chain-length growth' and the cleft 'is what preserves' make the causal link hard to parse."
  }
]

[
